/*
  Toggle.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0230 · Toggle (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/ui/Toggle.tsx) renders NO translatable copy of its own: the visible `label` is supplied
  by the caller, and the control's accessible name (`aria-labelledby`) is derived from that same
  caller-owned string. There are therefore no source `t()` keys to reproduce.

  The single key below is a native accessibility refinement: when no label is supplied the web sets
  `aria-labelledby` to `undefined`, leaving the switch with no accessible name, whereas the native
  surface always voices a name. It is resolved through the injected facade (with this English
  fallback) so no user-facing English is hardcoded in Swift. The per-surface table name ("Toggle")
  folds into the app Localizable.xcstrings master catalog at integration time.
*/

/* VoiceOver name for a switch that was given no visible label (native refinement; the web leaves an
   unlabeled switch's aria-labelledby undefined, so it has no accessible name). */
"toggle.accessibility.unlabeled" = "Toggle";
